## Why This Is Asked
The candidate demonstrates practical understanding of idempotence in multi-tenant CNFs via sidecar patterns and Redis TTLs.

## Key Concepts
- Idempotence and deduplication per tenant
- Redis SETNX with TTL for race-free dedupe
- Sidecar data flow and fallback handling

## Code Example
```go
// simplified sketch
package main
import "net/http"
func Handle(req *http.Request) {
  tenant := req.Header.Get("X-TENANT-ID")
  id := req.Header.Get("X-REQUEST-ID")
  key := tenant + ":" + id
  // pseudo Redis call with TTL 120s
  ok := redis.SetNX(key, "1", 120 * time.Second)
  if !ok {
    // respond 409 with {"error":"duplicate"}
    return
  }
  // forward to backend
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test dedupe behavior under high concurrency?
- How would you scale Redis for many tenants and ensure TTL correctness?

## Why This Is Asked
This question evaluates expertise in establishing end-to-end provenance for runtime plugins in multi-tenant CNF gateway environments, ensuring secure plugin lifecycle management with industry-standard tools.

## Key Concepts
- Cosign image signing with KMS-backed cryptographic keys
- SPDX SBOM generation and attachment to plugin images
- Per-tenant plugin policy enforcement via ConfigMap allowlists
- Admission webhook validation for signed plugin loading
- Gateway status API integration for provenance visibility
- Namespace-scoped validation with minimal deployment footprint

## Code Example
```go
// Admission webhook validating signed plugin images per tenant
package main

func validatePluginImage(imageRef, tenantNamespace string) error {
    // Verify Cosign signature using KMS public key
    if !cosign.Verify(imageRef, kmsPublicKey) {
        return fmt.Errorf("unsigned plugin image: %s", imageRef)
    }

    // Validate SBOM presence and integrity
    if !sbom.Validate(imageRef) {
        return fmt.Errorf("missing or invalid SBOM for: %s", imageRef)
    }

    // Check against tenant-specific allowlist
    if !allowlist.Contains(tenantNamespace, imageRef) {
        return fmt.Errorf("plugin not in tenant allowlist: %s", imageRef)
    }
    return nil
}
```

## Follow-up Considerations
- Implement automated key rotation for long-term security
- Design plugin update workflows maintaining provenance continuity
- Configure monitoring for plugin compliance violations across tenants

